1)ARRAY
-Linear ds used to store multiple items of same type in continuous memory location
-disadvantage-fixed size in most languages (altho python has dynamic allocation)
             -homogeneous, hance lack of flexibility(can be solved using referrential array)
             **A referential array is an array that stores memory addresses (references or pointers) to objects, rather than storing the actual data objects themselves side by side in memory

2)LINKED LIST
-its a collection of nodes, nodes have data and address of next node, first node is head and last is tail which has null for address
-stores data in non continous locations

difference b/w array and LL => array needs continous free m/m while LL does not

3)STACK
-uses LIFO
-ds that is open ended from one side and closed from the other and all operations happen from top
-possible operations are push, pop, peek, isempty, size
